From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:19:14 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add GSWIP-3.0 MDIO bus driver

Add an of_mdiobus driver for the MDIO master embedded in the
GSWIP-3.0 TOP register block (GSWT_MD* registers of the GSW-L
instance). Points hard-won on real silicon:

 - The GSWIP-3.0 master lives in the GSWT_MDIO/GSWT_MDC block, not
   the GSWIP-2.x MMDIO block the register names suggest; accesses
   use __raw_readl/__raw_writel (native big-endian MMIO).

 - MDC_CFG_1 fields must be written in the vendor order
   (FREQ, then MCEN, then RES release) or the master-clock enable
   does not latch; the busy flag (MBUSY) must be honored around
   every transaction, with a self-calibrated ctrl-word convention
   matching the vendor driver.

 - The hardware link poller (MDC auto-polling of the PHY link
   bits) is enabled, replacing any software forcing of
   PHY_ADDR/MAC_CTRL link state - the switch MACs take link
   directly from the poller.

 - PHY fixups applied at attach: a proper BMCR soft-reset and
   de-isolate (the vendor phylib did this on every attach), zeroed
   EEE advertisement, and the 1000BASE-T master-bias bit - all
   taken from the vendor driver's PHY setup; without them the link
   is unstable against some peers.

 - One-shot at first bring-up: re-initialize the switch core under
   an established PHY link via gsw_hw_reinit_gswl() and then re-arm
   the MDIO master/poller, which is the order the vendor's
   GSW_HW_Init runs in.

 - PHY enumeration waits for the GPHY firmware loader before
   scanning the bus.

The bus driver ships in the GPHY firmware loader's module, not in the
switch composite: it waits on xrx500_gphy_fw_is_loaded(), which stays
an intra-module call that way. gsw_hw_reinit_gswl() crosses a module
boundary as a result and is exported.

New driver written for this port against the register layout of the
AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release (Linux 4.9.198) switch-api headers
(gsw_reg_top.h).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/Makefile b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/Makefile
